  n<// Master AXI Address Channel> u<2> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<3> l<2:1> el<2:30>
  n<// This module performs a minimal AxADDR handshake, with the minimum number of> u<3> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<4> l<4:1> el<4:79>
  n<// parameters and settings possible (no LOCK, CACHE, PROT, REGION, ID, etc...).> u<4> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<5> l<5:1> el<5:80>
  n<// All transfers are AXI word-wide.> u<5> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<6> l<6:1> el<6:36>
  n<// There are two interfaces: System and Control.> u<6> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<7> l<8:1> el<8:49>
  n<// The System interface is where the host system sets the parameters for the> u<7> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<8> l<10:1> el<10:77>
  n<// transaction. The address, burst length, and burst type are all set by> u<8> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<9> l<11:1> el<11:73>
  n<// pulsing their _wren signal for one cycle. These parameters are persistent.> u<9> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<10> l<12:1> el<12:78>
  n<// Then system_start must be pulsed high for one cycle. The system_ready flag> u<10> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<11> l<13:1> el<13:78>
  n<// will go high when the transaction is done and stay high until a new> u<11> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<12> l<14:1> el<14:71>
  n<// transaction is started.> u<12> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<13> l<15:1> el<15:27>
  n<// The Control interface is internal to the AXI transactor and is controlled> u<13> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<14> l<17:1> el<17:77>
  n<// by another AXI sequencer, which allows the channel to begin operating by> u<14> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<15> l<18:1> el<18:76>
  n<// raising and holding control_enable high, until control_done also goes high> u<15> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<16> l<19:1> el<19:78>
  n<// to signal completion, then both go low. It functions just like> u<16> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<17> l<20:1> el<20:66>
  n<// a valid/ready handshake, thus it is an error to drop control_enable before> u<17> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<18> l<21:1> el<21:78>
  n<// control_done is asserted.> u<18> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<19> l<22:1> el<22:29>
  n<// Once both the System and Control interfaces are active, the address> u<19> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<20> l<24:1> el<24:71>
  n<// transaction begins and any signaling on the system interface is ignored> u<20> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<21> l<25:1> el<25:75>
  n<// until system_ready is raised. Thus, system_ready must be initialized high> u<21> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<22> l<26:1> el<26:77>
  n<// before the first system transaction to avoid a special case.> u<22> t<LINE_COMMENT> p<942> s<941> l<27:1> el<27:64>
